---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = 'August 12, 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | findbyface"
  description="How findbyface handles photos you upload, what data we collect, cookies, analytics, and your privacy rights."
  canonical="https://findbyface.org/privacy-policy/"
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <div class="page-head">
      <h1>Privacy <span class="gradient-text">Policy</span></h1>
      <p class="page-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how findbyface ("we", "us", "our") handles information when you
        use findbyface.org (the "Service"). By using the Service, you agree to the practices described
        here.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Photos you upload</h2>
      <p>
        When you upload a photo to run a face search, the image is processed to detect a face and
        generate a numeric facial descriptor used to rank visually similar creators. We do
        <strong>not</strong> store uploaded photos on our servers after the search is completed, and we
        do not use them to identify you or build a profile of you.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Usage data:</strong> pages visited, searches performed, and general interaction data, collected through analytics.</li>
        <li><strong>Device data:</strong> browser type, device type, and approximate region derived from your IP address.</li>
        <li><strong>Account data (optional):</strong> if you sign in, we receive your name, email, and profile image from your authentication provider.</li>
        <li><strong>Account search history:</strong> for signed-in users, we save submitted search terms, selected filters, result counts, and a limited set of result references so searches can be revisited across devices. We do not include uploaded photos or facial descriptors in search history.</li>
        <li><strong>Contact data:</strong> if you contact us, we receive the name, email, and message you provide.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use cookies and similar technologies, including Google Analytics, to understand how the
        Service is used and to improve it. You can control cookies through your browser settings.
        Analytics providers may process data according to their own privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h2>4. How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To operate and improve the face-search and discovery features.</li>
        <li>To provide private, cross-device search history for signed-in accounts.</li>
        <li>To measure performance, diagnose issues, and prevent abuse.</li>
        <li>To respond to your inquiries and support requests.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Sharing of information</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal information. We may share limited data with service providers
        (such as hosting, authentication, and analytics) who process it on our behalf, and where
        required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        Uploaded photos and facial descriptors are not retained after a search. Signed-in search
        history is retained until you delete individual searches, clear your history, or your
        account is deleted. Other data, such as analytics and contact messages, is retained only as
        long as necessary for the purposes described above.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, or delete your personal
        data. To make a request, contact us via our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Children</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is intended only for adults 18 years of age or older. We do not knowingly collect
        data from anyone under 18.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by the
        "Last updated" date above.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy? Reach us through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
